   221	### Step 6 — Wrap-up Loop
   222	
   223	**Definition.** Consolidate the artifacts from prior loops, clean up scratch state, and produce the session's deliverables.
   224	
   225	**Inputs.** `Idea`, `Plan`, `Results` from prior loops (or whichever subset exists if some loops aborted).
   226	
   227	**Output.** Doc updates (Principle 8), session report, project memory updates, handoff summary, metadata.
   228	
   229	**Loop iteration.** Rows 1-5 form one iteration. Row 5 decides whether to iterate (back to row 1) or exit the loop. Repeats up to `workflow.wrap-up.maxIterations` until `PASS`, `Skipped`, or cap exhausted.
   230	
   231	| # | Phase | Action | Refs | Agent |
   232	|---|---|---|---|---|
   233	| 1 | `DISCUSSION` | Construct the delegation prompt. In Chat Mode, confirm with the user. | [discussion](../discussion/SKILL.md), [delegation](../delegation/SKILL.md) | manager |
   234	| 2 | `WRAPUP` | Spawn `assistant` subagent(s). Consolidate artifacts; clean scratch state. | [wrap-up.md](workflow/wrap-up.md) | assistant |
   235	| 3 | `EVALUATION` | Run per `workflow.wrap-up.evaluate.mode`. | [evaluation.md](workflow/evaluation.md) | evaluator |
   236	| 4 | `MEMORIZATION` | Write session and project memory for this iteration — decisions, consolidation outcomes, eval findings, deferred items. | [memorization.md](workflow/memorization.md) | assistant |
   237	| 5 | `ITER / EXIT` | Decide based on verdict and budget. `PASS` or `Skipped` → exit with the deliverables (the session is complete). `REVISE`/`FAIL` with budget remaining → return to row 1 with findings appended. `REVISE`/`FAIL` with no budget → exit with abort. | — | manager |
