   240	
   241	| Mode | Context | Behavior at the `ITER / EXIT` exit of step `N` |
   242	|---|---|---|
   243	| Chat | Within a per-task slice (Step 2 → Step 4 → Step 5) | AskUserQuestion to confirm advance to the next slice-step; user may revise scope, abort, or branch. Step 3 transitions silently to `Skipped` — no user gate at that boundary. |
   244	| Chat | At task boundary (after task-record written) | AskUserQuestion: per-task user review gate — Next task / Revise / Wrap up. Only on "Wrap up" does the manager advance to Step 6. |
   245	| Auto | — | Auto-advance to step `N+1`. Halt only if a `maxIterations` abort makes downstream infeasible or a user-authority decision is required. |
